---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CapturePlaceholder from '../components/CapturePlaceholder.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Seculana — financial models that read like the plan"
  description="Seculana is a declarative language for financial models: accounts, taxes, life events, decisions and uncertainty written as the plan itself."
>
  <header class="site-header">
    <a class="wordmark" href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL} aria-label="Seculana home">Seculana</a>
    <nav aria-label="Primary">
      <a href="#idea">The idea</a>
      <a href="#proof">Proof</a>
      <a href="#roadmap">Roadmap</a>
      <a href="#join">Get involved</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">A language for money over time</p>
      <h1>Financial models that read like the plan, not like a spreadsheet.</h1>
      <p class="lede">This is the Phase 1 skeleton. The story, examples and authentic Seculana captures arrive increment by increment.</p>
      <div class="hero-code" aria-label="A small Seculana example">
        <pre><code><span>years 2026 to 2035</span>

<span>let Salary = @Salary * (1 + 3%) starting $95,000</span>
<span>let Saved  = Salary * 15%</span>

<span>balance Nest opening $40,000 growth 6% inflow Saved</span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="idea" class="section-shell placeholder-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Recognition</p>
      <h2>Money has state, rules, choices and consequences.</h2>
      <p>Balances, flows, taxes, priorities, scenarios and uncertainty belong in the model as financial ideas, not hidden plumbing.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="proof" class="section-shell placeholder-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Proof</p>
      <h2>The model can explain what happened.</h2>
      <CapturePlaceholder id="CAP-002" alt="Seculana Playground showing the financial story of a value for a specific year." />
    </section>

    <section id="roadmap" class="section-shell placeholder-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Road ahead</p>
      <h2>Built in small, testable phases.</h2>
      <p>Implemented work, recorded roadmap and exploratory frontier ideas will be shown as visibly different things.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="join" class="section-shell closing-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Invitation</p>
      <h2>Bring Seculana a hard financial model.</h2>
      <p>The public engagement path will be added once the product repository, licence and contribution channel are ready.</p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer section-shell">
    <p>Seculana-Web is being built in public, one reviewable increment at a time.</p>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>
